WorkflowDependencies: SDD

Purpose:
  Defines dependencies between workflow stages. Stage dependencies
  are distinct from task dependencies — they define which stages must
  complete before others can begin, not which tasks block which tasks.

StageDependencies:
  DISCOVER -> ANALYZE:
    Type: SEQUENTIAL
    Condition: always

  ANALYZE -> ARCHITECT:
    Type: SEQUENTIAL
    Condition: architecture_required = true

  ANALYZE -> DECIDE:
    Type: SEQUENTIAL
    Condition: simple_change = true

  ARCHITECT -> DECIDE:
    Type: SEQUENTIAL
    Condition: always

  DECIDE -> PLAN:
    Type: SEQUENTIAL
    Condition: always

  PLAN -> BDD:
    Type: SEQUENTIAL
    Condition: always

  BDD -> DEVELOP:
    Type: SEQUENTIAL
    Condition: always

  DEVELOP -> REVIEW:
    Type: SEQUENTIAL
    Condition: always

  REVIEW -> TEST:
    Type: SEQUENTIAL
    Condition: always

  TEST -> SECURITY:
    Type: SEQUENTIAL
    Condition: security_required = true

  SECURITY -> DEPLOY:
    Type: SEQUENTIAL
    Condition: security_passed = true

  DEPLOY -> OBSERVE:
    Type: SEQUENTIAL
    Condition: always

  OBSERVE -> VERIFY:
    Type: SEQUENTIAL
    Condition: always

  VERIFY -> DONE:
    Type: SEQUENTIAL
    Condition: always

ConditionalStages:
  SECURITY:
    Condition: security_required = true
    Else: skip

  LOAD:
    Condition: scale = L4 or performance_critical = true
    Else: skip

  PENTEST:
    Condition: security_level = HIGH or CRITICAL
    Else: skip

ParallelStages:
  - FE and MD can run in parallel after API contract is ready
  - UNIT and CONTRACT can run in parallel after DEVELOP

CriticalPath:
  - For feature work: BDD -> DEVELOP -> REVIEW -> TEST -> VERIFY
  - For security work: BDD -> DEVELOP -> REVIEW -> TEST -> SECURITY -> VERIFY
  - For infrastructure: PLAN -> DEPLOY -> OBSERVE -> VERIFY

State: +
  